{
  "id": "COMPOUND:21717 - PROTEIN:710",
  "verbalization": "Ligustrone A is implicated in the target relationship with ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1 through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Ligustrone A acts as a target for multiple compounds, including Cis-Bis(Methylthio)Silvatin and 6-Ethyl-4-hydroxy-5-methyl-3-[[2,4,6-trihydroxy-3-(3-methyl-2-butenyl)-5-(2-methyl-1-oxopropyl)phenyl]methyl]-2 h-pyran-2-one, which in turn target the ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1. These compounds are likely involved in mechanisms that modulate the activity of the ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1, possibly through direct interaction or indirect regulatory pathways. The presence of multiple targets and the involvement of diverse compounds suggest a complex network of interactions, where Ligustrone A may serve as a key mediator in the biological effects of these compounds. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Ligustrone A to play a central role in the regulation of ATP-binding cassette sub-family A member 1, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
